rface carburettor, later from a float carburettor." ] } ], "note": "Benz built 67 Velos in 1894 and 134 in 1895, and about 1,200 Velo and Comfortable cars by 1902, at 2,000 marks. A Velo took part in the Paris–Rouen run of 1894. A third gear and reverse were optional from 1896 and standard from 1900.", "unverified": [ "Pulley and sprocket sizes, and the low-gear speed (about 12 km/h)", "Laden mass (two people aboard), rolling resistance and driveline efficiency", "Engine, flywheel and countershaft positions, conrod length", "Ghost-body outline (traced from the photo)", "Room: Legend 1" ] }
